// TEST: T^0 call whose later argument would NARROW (rejects)
// ERROR: BL3999
// ERROR-CONTAINS: must agree EXACTLY
// ============================================================================
// Arguments sharing one type variable agree EXACTLY (formalism 2.4): no
// argument converts implicitly, in either order. Here argument 1 makes `T`
// Int64 and argument 2 is a Float64 -- the Int64 monomorph would have to
// NARROW the 2.5. The reverse order (`add0(2.5, 3)`) used to be accepted
// because the Int64 WIDENED into the Float64 monomorph; it is refused too
// (functions/401), and 044 pins the explicit conversion.
// ============================================================================
function add0(a: T^0, b: T^0) -> T^0 = a + b

let r = add0(3, 2.5)
